I'm Kim Mills. Our guest today is Dr. Kristen Shockley, an associate professor of psychology at the University of Georgia. Dr. Shockley has spent her career studying the University of Georgia. intersection of work and family life. She's conducted research on how employees balance work and family demands, how work family conflict affects people's health, and how dual career couples navigate work and family roles. When the COVID-19 crisis hit, she realized that the upheaval caused by school and office closures made those questions even more pressing, and she set out to investigate how workers are adjusting. Welcome to speaking of psychology, Dr. Shockley. Thank you for having me.
我是金·米尔斯。我们今天的嘉宾是佐治亚大学心理学副教授克里斯汀·肖克利博士。肖克利博士的职业生涯一直致力于研究工作与家庭生活的交集。她对员工如何平衡工作与家庭需求、工作与家庭冲突如何影响人们的健康，以及双职工夫妻如何处理工作与家庭角色进行了研究。当新冠疫情爆发时，她意识到学校和办公室关闭所带来的动荡使这些问题变得更加紧迫，于是她着手调查员工们是如何适应的。欢迎来到《心理学谈话》，肖克利博士。谢谢你邀请我。

